From 30c027135e6ba41dceec165eeb70c2557daf5735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psyche <hkjeon13@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:00:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] perf(cuda): add a packed-heads D128 partial-state producer
 (four lanes per query head)

One warp serves all eight query heads of a KV head. Each lane keeps the
partial sums of the eight original lanes it stands for and folds them in the
original tree order, so states are bit-identical while using an eighth of the
threads. Exposed as an additional launch geometry; the GPU test compares every
workspace byte against the per-query-head launch. Not yet used by the runtime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
